{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "diffusers-edge-t2i",
      "prompt": "Generate ONE image with the Cosmos3 diffusers path on this machine's single GPU: run text2image with nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge (guardrails disabled for this smoke) using the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json), and save the image as outputs/t2i_edge.png.",
      "expected_outcome": "A non-trivial t2i_edge.png generated by Cosmos3-Edge via diffusers exists in the artifacts outputs dir, and result_summary.md records model, settings, runtime, and peak CUDA memory.",
      "assertions": [
        "A dedicated Python environment was created for diffusers and the generation ran from it, not the system python",
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge was the checkpoint used, loaded in bfloat16 on the GPU",
        "outputs/t2i_edge.png exists, is a valid non-empty image, and was produced by the pipeline run recorded in the transcript (not copied or fabricated)",
        "The skill's documented diffusers workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md reports the settings, wall-clock time, and GPU memory actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/t2i_edge.png",
          "min_bytes": 20000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "env setup",
        "model load",
        "generation",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "diffusers-edge-t2v",
      "prompt": "Generate ONE short video with the Cosmos3 diffusers path on this machine's single GPU: run text2video with nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge (guardrails disabled for this smoke) using the skill's bundled text2video prompt (assets/prompts/text2video/robot_kitchen.json) and the skill's bundled text2video negative prompt (assets/negative_prompts/text2video/neg_prompt.json) at Edge's documented video settings, and save the clip as outputs/t2v_edge.mp4. Record the clip's resolution, frame count and duration (ffprobe) in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "A non-trivial t2v_edge.mp4 generated by Cosmos3-Edge via diffusers (Edge video regime: 832x480, about 121 frames at 24 fps) exists in the artifacts outputs dir, and result_summary.md records settings, wall-clock time, peak CUDA memory and the ffprobe stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "A dedicated Python environment was created for diffusers and the generation ran from it, not the system python",
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge was the checkpoint used, loaded in bfloat16 on the GPU, with the text2video negative prompt asset applied",
        "outputs/t2v_edge.mp4 exists and is a valid non-empty MP4 of about 121 frames at 24 fps and 832x480 (ffprobe output in the transcript), produced by the pipeline run recorded in the transcript (not copied or fabricated)",
        "The skill's documented diffusers workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md reports the settings, wall-clock time, GPU memory and ffprobe facts actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/t2v_edge.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 200000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "env setup",
        "model load",
        "generation",
        "verify (ffprobe) + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "framework-edge-t2i",
      "prompt": "Generate ONE image with the cosmos_framework inference path on this machine's single GPU. Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill; run Cosmos3-Edge text2image (guardrails disabled, seed 0) using the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json), saving the generated image under outputs/.",
      "expected_outcome": "The framework torchrun inference completes on one GPU with Cosmos3-Edge from a fresh clone of the public framework main and produces an image under the artifacts outputs dir; result_summary.md records the exact command and runtime.",
      "assertions": [
        "Inference ran through cosmos_framework.scripts.inference via torchrun with --nproc-per-node=1 and checkpoint Cosmos3-Edge",
        "The framework checkout used for setup and inference is a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main (the transcript shows the clone), not the skill snapshot",
        "A payload JSON was built around the prompt asset per the documented schema (not the raw prompt file passed directly)",
        "A generated image exists under outputs/ and is non-empty",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md contains the exact command line used and the measured runtime"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "payload build",
        "inference run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm-omni-edge-t2i",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge with vLLM-Omni (guardrails disabled) and generate ONE image through its HTTP API from the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json); save the returned image as outputs/t2i_vllm.png, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "The vLLM-Omni server comes up, serves one t2i request from the bundled prompt, and t2i_vllm.png plus a summary with server/readiness/latency details exist in artifacts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The vLLM-Omni server was started with the documented image and flags and reached readiness before any generation request",
        "The t2i request used the skill's bundled robot_draping.json prompt asset",
        "outputs/t2i_vllm.png exists and is a valid non-empty image returned by the server",
        "The server was stopped/cleaned up at the end",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, and request latency"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/t2i_vllm.png",
          "min_bytes": 20000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "generation request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sglang-edge-t2i",
      "prompt": "Serve the smallest single-GPU Cosmos3 generator checkpoint with SGLang (guardrails disabled) and generate ONE image through its API from the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json). Poll the server's health endpoint until ready before sending the request. Save the image as outputs/t2i_sglang.png, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "An SGLang-served Cosmos3 generator produces one image from the bundled prompt; image, summary, and transcript are in artifacts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The server reached a healthy state before the generation request was sent",
        "The generation used the skill's bundled robot_draping.json prompt asset",
        "outputs/t2i_sglang.png exists and is a valid non-empty image",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md records checkpoint, server command, time-to-ready, and request latency"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/t2i_sglang.png",
          "min_bytes": 20000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "generation request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "trtllm-edge-t2i",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Edge with TensorRT-LLM (trtllm-serve, guardrails disabled) and generate ONE image via its client payload flow from the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json); save the image as outputs/t2i_trtllm.png, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "trtllm-serve hosts Cosmos3-Edge, one t2i request succeeds using the bundled prompt, and image + summary + transcript are in artifacts.",
      "assertions": [
        "trtllm-serve was launched for Cosmos3-Edge and became ready before requests",
        "Guardrails were disabled via the documented mechanism rather than acquiring gated access",
        "outputs/t2i_trtllm.png exists and is a valid non-empty image",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md records the serve command, readiness time, and request latency"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/t2i_trtllm.png",
          "min_bytes": 20000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "generation request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "distilled-trtllm-t2i",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Super-Text2Image-4Step with trtllm-serve (guardrails disabled) and run one t2i_distilled generation (single 1024x1024 image, 4 steps) from the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json); save the image as outputs/t2i_4step.png. The bf16 checkpoint is ~130GB: check the GPU memory actually available on this machine and make a genuine attempt to serve within it (reduced-precision/FP8 weights, host offload, a smaller max batch or resolution, or whatever the skill documents) before concluding it cannot run. Only after a real serving attempt has failed, record the exact blocker, the measured memory numbers and the resource requirement in result_summary.md \u2014 never fabricate output.",
      "expected_outcome": "t2i_4step.png generated by the 4-step distilled model exists in artifacts; only if real serving attempts on this GPU fail does result_summary.md instead document the precise blocker with measured numbers.",
      "assertions": [
        "The run produced outputs/t2i_4step.png from the 4-step model, or \u2014 only after at least one genuine attempt to serve it on this GPU (reduced precision, offload or a smaller configuration) \u2014 documented the concrete blocker with measured evidence",
        "No output was fabricated: any image present traces to a real server response in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md states the checkpoint size and the GPU resources available vs required",
        "The documented t2i_distilled client flow was used"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start attempt",
        "generation or blocker analysis",
        "summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nim-generator-i2v",
      "prompt": "Launch the Cosmos3 Generator NIM container (guardrails disabled) and generate ONE short image2video clip through its API using the skill's bundled image2video prompt (assets/prompts/image2video/car_driving.json) with its reference image (assets/images/image2video/car_driving.jpg); save the video as outputs/i2v_nim.mp4, then stop the container. The Generator NIM serves Text2Video and Image2Video only. Make the NIM actually serve on this GPU: inspect the profiles available for this hardware and select a compatible one explicitly (NIM_MODEL_PROFILE or the documented equivalent) instead of relying on auto-selection, and relaunch with corrected flags if the first launch fails. Only if the image or NGC access is unavailable, or no profile can run on this GPU after real attempts, record the exact blocker in result_summary.md \u2014 never fabricate output.",
      "expected_outcome": "i2v_nim.mp4 generated via a ready NIM endpoint exists in artifacts; only if no compatible profile can run here after real attempts does result_summary.md instead document the precise blocker.",
      "assertions": [
        "The run produced outputs/i2v_nim.mp4 from a ready NIM endpoint, or \u2014 only after explicit profile selection and at least one corrected relaunch \u2014 documented the concrete blocker with evidence",
        "No output was fabricated: any video present traces to a real endpoint response in the transcript",
        "An Image2Video request was used (the Generator NIM does not expose text2image)",
        "result_summary.md records the container image, readiness outcome, and request latency or blocker"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "container launch",
        "readiness",
        "generation or blocker analysis",
        "summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "diffusers-nano-t2i",
      "prompt": "Generate ONE image with the Cosmos3 diffusers path on this machine's single GPU using the larger Nano checkpoint: run text2image with nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano (guardrails disabled for this smoke) using the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json), and save the image as outputs/t2i_nano.png. Cosmos3-Nano is ~31.5 GB in bf16 \u2014 check the GPU memory available on this machine and follow the skill's model-size guidance (offload or reduced precision if needed) so that generation actually runs, recording peak memory in result_summary.md. Only if generation fails after real attempts, record the exact blocker and memory numbers \u2014 never fabricate output.",
      "expected_outcome": "A non-trivial t2i_nano.png generated by Cosmos3-Nano via diffusers exists in the artifacts outputs dir, and result_summary.md records model, settings, runtime, and peak CUDA memory (a documented blocker is acceptable only after real generation attempts failed).",
      "assertions": [
        "A dedicated Python environment was created for diffusers and the generation ran from it, not the system python",
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano was the checkpoint used, loaded on the GPU following the skill's model-size guidance for the memory available",
        "outputs/t2i_nano.png exists as a valid non-empty image produced by the pipeline run recorded in the transcript (a documented memory blocker is acceptable only after real generation attempts failed)",
        "No output was fabricated: any image present traces to a real pipeline run in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md reports the settings, wall-clock time, and GPU memory actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "env setup",
        "model load",
        "generation or blocker analysis",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "framework-nano-t2i",
      "prompt": "Generate ONE image with the cosmos_framework inference path on this machine's single GPU using the Nano checkpoint. Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill; run Cosmos3-Nano text2image (guardrails disabled, seed 0) using the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json), saving the generated image under outputs/. Cosmos3-Nano is ~31.5 GB in bf16 \u2014 check the GPU memory available on this machine and follow the skill's model-size guidance so that inference actually runs; only if it fails after real attempts, record the exact blocker and memory numbers in result_summary.md \u2014 never fabricate output.",
      "expected_outcome": "The framework torchrun inference completes on one GPU with Cosmos3-Nano from a fresh clone of the public framework main and produces an image under the artifacts outputs dir; result_summary.md records the exact command and runtime (a documented blocker is acceptable only after real attempts failed).",
      "assertions": [
        "Inference ran through cosmos_framework.scripts.inference via torchrun with --nproc-per-node=1 and checkpoint Cosmos3-Nano",
        "The framework checkout used for setup and inference is a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main (the transcript shows the clone), not the skill snapshot",
        "A payload JSON was built around the prompt asset per the documented schema (not the raw prompt file passed directly)",
        "A generated image exists under outputs/ and is non-empty (a documented memory blocker is acceptable only after real inference attempts failed)",
        "No output was fabricated: any image present traces to a real inference run in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md contains the exact command line used and the measured runtime"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "payload build",
        "inference or blocker analysis",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trtllm-nano-t2i",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with TensorRT-LLM (trtllm-serve, guardrails disabled) using the skill's documented single-GPU Nano serving configuration, and generate ONE image via its client payload flow using the skill's bundled text2image prompt (assets/prompts/text2image/robot_draping.json); save the image as outputs/t2i_trtllm_nano.png, then stop the server. Cosmos3-Nano is ~31.5 GB in bf16 plus serving overhead \u2014 check the GPU memory available and tune the documented serving configuration (max batch size, KV/workspace fraction, warmup resolution, precision) so the server actually comes up. Only if it still cannot start after real tuning attempts, record the exact blocker and memory numbers in result_summary.md \u2014 never fabricate output.",
      "expected_outcome": "trtllm-serve hosts Cosmos3-Nano on one GPU and one t2i request succeeds from the bundled prompt; image plus summary and transcript are in artifacts (a documented serving blocker is acceptable only after real tuning attempts failed).",
      "assertions": [
        "trtllm-serve was launched for Cosmos3-Nano using the skill's documented single-GPU Nano configuration",
        "Guardrails were disabled via the documented mechanism rather than acquiring gated access",
        "outputs/t2i_trtllm_nano.png exists as a valid non-empty image returned by the server (a documented serving blocker is acceptable only after real tuning attempts failed)",
        "No output was fabricated: any image present traces to a real server response in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md records the serve command, readiness time or failure point, and request latency or blocker"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness or blocker analysis",
        "generation",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN",
    "GITHUB_TOKEN",
    "NGC_API_KEY"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 60,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
